(Stage 1e3 - `is not nothing` is the negated equality route. A present
 number, text, and boolean are all not nothing; a `value` holding a real
 number is not nothing. Acceptance: the four lines.)

if 7 is not nothing, print "7 is not nothing".
if "x" is not nothing, print "x is not nothing".
if true is not nothing, print "true is not nothing".

To "check" with a value called "v".
  if v is not nothing, print "v is not nothing".

"check" of 42.